.TH snip-man 1  "snip 0.6.0" "Snip Manual"
.SH "NAME"
snip\-man \- install, inspect, and export manual pages
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBsnip man\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
\fBsnip man path\fR [\fB\-\-prefix\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
\fBsnip man install\fR [\fB\-\-prefix\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
\fBsnip man uninstall\fR [\fB\-\-prefix\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
\fBsnip man show\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPAGE\fR] 
\fBsnip man generate\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIDIRECTORY\fR> 
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Inspect and manage the manual pages embedded in the snip binary. path prints the installation directory, install writes pages and a hash manifest, uninstall removes only unchanged recorded pages, show opens an embedded page with the system viewer, and generate exports the embedded set.
.PP
Package\-managed binaries should install manual pages through the same package manager. install refuses an existing unrecorded page unless \-\-force is given. During upgrades it removes obsolete recorded pages whose hashes still match and keeps modified pages recorded for a later uninstall.
.PP
Global options are described in snip(1).
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "snip man"
.PP
Install, inspect, or export the embedded manual pages
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS "snip man path"
.PP
Print the resolved man hierarchy root containing man1, man5, and man7
.TP
\fB\-\-prefix\fR \fI<PREFIX>\fR
Resolve the directory below PREFIX/share instead of the user data directory
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS "snip man install"
.PP
Install all manual pages
.TP
\fB\-\-prefix\fR \fI<PREFIX>\fR
Install below PREFIX/share instead of the user data directory
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Replace pages not recorded in snip\*(Aqs installation manifest
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS "snip man uninstall"
.PP
Remove unmodified pages recorded by snip
.TP
\fB\-\-prefix\fR \fI<PREFIX>\fR
Uninstall below PREFIX/share instead of the user data directory
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS "snip man show"
.PP
Show an embedded manual page with the system man viewer
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIPAGE\fR]
Page stem or explicit page, such as snip, sniplib, or config.5
.SS "snip man generate"
.PP
Export all embedded manual pages to a directory
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIDIRECTORY\fR>
Destination root; pages are written below man1, man5, and man7
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
Install pages for the current user and show the create page:
.RS 4
.nf
snip man install
snip man show create
.fi
.RE
.PP
Export all embedded pages and install below a prefix:
.RS 4
.nf
snip man generate ./generated\-man
snip man install \-\-prefix /usr/local
.fi
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR snip (1),
.BR snip\-config (5),
.BR snip\-agents (7)
